      "Nordic-style welfare states are frequently called socialist in U.S. debate, but they generally preserve private ownership, competitive firms, markets, and international trade while using high taxation and broad public benefits to redistribute income and reduce insecurity.",
      "This distinction matters. A capitalist economy with strong social insurance is institutionally different from an economy in which the state or workers collectively own most productive assets.",
