      "The Russian Revolution of 1917 produced the first durable state governed by a communist party. The Soviet system later combined extensive state ownership, central planning, one-party rule, censorship, security institutions, and political repression. Communist revolutions or governments later emerged in China, Cuba, Vietnam, North Korea, and other countries, each with different institutions and historical conditions.",
      "Some communist-led states achieved rapid industrialization, expanded literacy, or provided broad basic services. They also frequently produced severe repression, political imprisonment, restricted speech, economic shortage, famine or catastrophic policy failure in particular periods, and highly concentrated political authority.",
