      '<strong data-case-part="true" class="text-stone-100">5. Political Language and Ambiguity</strong>',
      "“Communism” is frequently used to describe any large government program, which empties the term of meaning. Conversely, defenders sometimes define communism only as the ideal final stage and treat every historical failure as categorically unrelated. A useful analysis has to keep the distinction between theory and historical regime while still asking whether the pathway proposed by the theory systematically creates particular risks.",
      '<strong data-case-part="true" class="text-stone-100">6. Argument Deconstructions</strong>',
